Article 1 Definitions
------------------------------------------------------------------------

1.1 "The Software"
    means the source code, binary files, documentation,
    configuration files, resource files, sample code,
    test cases, and any part or derivative work thereof
    attached to this license.

1.2 "Derivative Work"
    means any work based on all or part of the Software,
    created through modification, translation, adaptation,
    reorganization, extension, deletion, merging, linking,
    or any other means.

1.3 "Distribute"
    means to provide the Software or its Derivative Work
    to any third party in any form, including copying,
    transmission, uploading, downloading, public release,
    sharing, mirroring, packaging, integrated release,
    or providing through network services or APIs.

1.4 "Contribution"
    means any code, documentation, translation, design,
    suggestion, issue report, test case, patch, or any
    other content you submit to the Software.

1.5 "You"
    means any individual or legal entity exercising
    rights granted by this license.

1.6 "Copyright Holder"
    means the original author and any subsequent
    copyright owner of the Software.

1.7 "Corresponding Source"
    means all source code required to generate, install,
    run, and modify the Software or a Derivative Work,
    including build scripts, configuration files, and
    interface definitions.

1.8 "Static Linking"
    means incorporating the Software into a Derivative Work
    in a manner that produces a single executable or
    binary artifact, including but not limited to
    compilation, static library linking, or code
    generation that embeds the Software.

1.9 "Dynamic Linking"
    means incorporating the Software into a Derivative Work
    as a separate library, module, or plugin loaded at
    runtime, without embedding the Software's code into
    the primary executable.

1.10 "Network Service"
     means providing the Software or a Derivative Work
     to third parties as a hosted service, API, or
     software-as-a-service, where users interact with
     the Software over a network but do not receive
     a copy of the Software itself.

1.11 "Optional AI Clause"
     means the additional provisions set out in
     Article 20, which the Copyright Holder may
     elect to apply to the Software by including
     a notice in the Software's documentation.


