Article 12 Reinstatement After Termination
------------------------------------------------------------------------

12.1 Automatic Reinstatement Period
     (a) If you violate this license, you have 60 days
         from the date of violation to cure the
         violation and reinstate your license
         automatically.
     (b) To cure, you must:
         (i) stop all violating conduct;
         (ii) restore compliance with this license;
         (iii) notify the Copyright Holder in writing
               of the cure.
     (c) If you cure within 60 days, your license is
         automatically reinstated as if the violation
         had not occurred.
     (d) This automatic reinstatement is available
         only for the first violation.

12.2 Discretionary Reinstatement
     (a) If you fail to cure within 60 days, or if
         you have previously cured a violation,
         reinstatement requires the Copyright
         Holder's written consent.
     (b) The Copyright Holder may grant or deny
         reinstatement at its sole discretion.

12.3 No Retroactivity
     Reinstatement does not retroactively cover
     prior violations.


