Article 20 Optional AI Clause
------------------------------------------------------------------------

This article applies only if the Copyright Holder
includes a notice in the Software's documentation
stating that the Optional AI Clause is enabled.

20.1 Model Derivative Work
     If the Optional AI Clause is enabled, a "Model
     Derivative Work" means any model, weight,
     parameter, embedding, or generative system
     arising from:
     (a) training using the Software as a training
         framework, inference engine, or data
         processing pipeline;
     (b) fine-tuning, distillation, quantization,
         pruning, or merging of the Software where
         the Software itself is a model or weight;
     (c) training on synthetic data generated by
         the Software.

20.2 Open Source Obligation
     (a) If you distribute a Model Derivative Work,
         you must make public:
         (i) the model weights or parameters;
         (ii) the training code used to produce
              the model.
     (b) You are not required to disclose training
         data or data sources.
     (c) Internal use of a Model Derivative Work
         does not trigger this obligation.
     (d) Inference-only use (no training or
         fine-tuning) does not produce a Model
         Derivative Work.

20.3 Scope
     This article applies only to the extent the
     Optional AI Clause is enabled. If not enabled,
     this article has no effect.


